The statistics dept. seminars can be abstruse, but this week’s looks like it may be worthwhile if you use splines. Details below.

Dr. Wang’s methods are implemented in the assist <http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/assist/index.html> R package, for which an overview and manual are available on his website <http://www.pstat.ucsb.edu/faculty/yuedong/software.html>. I note that his book <http://www.pstat.ucsb.edu/faculty/yuedong/book/book.html> on these methods is available digitally through the UCD library <http://harvest.lib.ucdavis.edu/F/?func=direct&doc_number=003312537&local_base=UCD01PUB>.
