Dan,

I had to ask around to get some more history. The parent(s) was a hybrid that was selfed to F2 and then a series of F7 RILs were developed from there. I think I have a genotype profile for the original hybrid. It would likely be heterozygous for many SNPs, so I'm not sure how the recoding would go.

I have genome anchors for most of the SNPs in the chip.

I was just trying to get to grips with the data and there are a lot of monomorphic markers, heterozygous markers, and NA results "-/-".

BSA <- read.delim("SNPdata.txt", stringsAsFactors=FALSE)

#vector to store number of levels
levelNum <- rep(0, ncol(BSA)-2)

for (i in 3:ncol(BSA)) {
